   "id": "us-cpi-fed-hike",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Firm October inflation pushes a December Fed hike to near-certainty",
   "when": "Tue 10 Nov · 08:30 ET",
   "what": "US consumer prices rose 0.4% in October after 0.6% in September; core prices rose 0.3%. Energy rose 0.7% and food 0.5%. Forecasts were 0.3% and 0.2%. Fed officials Waller and Logan then backed hikes, with Logan saying the pace may need to quicken. The 10-year yield ended near 4.98%, up 12 basis points, and the S&P 500 closed down 0.38% at 7,521. Nasdaq fell 0.74%.",
   "why": "Higher rates weigh on large US shares, including your S&P 500 funds and Apple, Meta and Tesla. ES-US500RMF and K-USA-A(D) are priced at 6 Nov NAVs this morning. The S&P 500 has risen about 1.95% since then, and that is not in their numbers yet. The dashboard refreshes again at 11:30.",
